Student residence policy (plain-text source fixture)

The residence policy governs room allocation, check-in, conduct, safety, and checkout. Students apply online during the published application window and receive an allocation notice before the semester begins. Check-in requires a valid student identity document and completion of the residence agreement. Residents must keep shared areas clean, follow quiet hours, protect access cards, and report maintenance or safety issues promptly. Guests are allowed only under the registration rules of the residence hall.
The residence office may investigate violations and may provide a warning, charge a repair cost, or terminate an agreement for serious misconduct. A resident who leaves must return keys and complete checkout. Deposits are handled according to the inspection record. Emergency instructions are posted in each building, and residents should contact campus security for immediate danger.
Operational guidance: residents must not lend access cards, alter rooms, obstruct fire equipment, or create hazards. Maintenance requests include a room number and clear description. The office communicates inspections and repairs when practical. Questions about agreements, charges, or appeals go to the official residence office account. These requirements support a safe, fair, and quiet environment for every resident.
